return [
    'Dashboard and Workspace' => [

        'Dashboard' => [
            'body' => '<p>The IFRS 9 ECL Dashboard is the one-page position of the loan book for a reporting period: how much is owed, how much provision is held against it, how the book splits across the three IFRS 9 stages, and how these have moved against an earlier period. It is the landing page after sign-in and the first thing management, finance and risk staff read. To return to it, press <b>Dashboard</b> at the top of the sidebar or the logo. Everything on the page is read from the database for the period, portfolio and comparison you choose in the green filter bar; only periods for which ECL has been calculated are offered.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li>Page title <b>IFRS 9 ECL Dashboard</b> with the round green help button beside it.</li><li><b>Filter bar</b> (green pill, top right) with three drop-downs: <b>Reporting Period</b> (calendar icon; the latest calculated period is selected by default), <b>Portfolio</b> (layers icon; <b>All portfolios</b> or one loan portfolio) and <b>Compare To</b> (calendar icon; <b>Previous period</b>, meaning the closest earlier calculated period, or any other period). Changing any of them reloads the whole page.</li><li>A context line: <b>Showing 2023-12 · portfolio Agriculture · compared to 2023-11</b>.</li><li><b>Six KPI tiles</b>, each with an icon, a compact value, the exact amount in small grey text and either a change chip or a note: <b>Total Exposure (EAD)</b>, <b>Total ECL</b>, <b>ECL Coverage</b>, <b>Stage 3 Exposure</b>, <b>Weighted PD</b>, <b>Weighted LGD</b>.</li><li><b>Three stage cards</b>: <b>Stage 1</b> (green, badge <b>Performing</b>), <b>Stage 2</b> (gold, badge <b>Underperforming</b>), <b>Stage 3</b> (red, badge <b>Non-performing</b>). Each shows <b>Exposure (EAD)</b>, then <b>ECL</b>, <b>PD</b> and <b>Share of book</b>.</li><li><b>Portfolio Composition by Stage</b>: a doughnut with a legend for Stage 1, 2 and 3 and a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle. The table has the columns <b>Stage</b>, <b>EAD</b>, <b>Share</b>. Hovering a segment shows the amount and its share.</li><li><b>ECL Coverage Trend</b>: a green line chart of coverage per period with two range selectors (<b>From Jan 2023</b>, <b>From the start</b> or <b>From</b> any period; <b>To latest</b> or <b>To</b> any period), a <b>Chart</b> / <b>Table</b> toggle and a caption giving the range shown. The selected reporting period is marked with a gold dot. The table has the columns <b>Period</b>, <b>ECL %</b>.</li><li><b>Portfolio Summary</b> table with the note <b>Values in USD</b> (your organisation currency) and the columns <b>Metric</b>, <b>Current (2023-12)</b>, <b>Compare To (2023-11)</b>, <b>Change</b>, <b>Status</b>. The last three appear only when a comparison period exists. Rows: <b>Total EAD</b>, <b>Weighted PD</b>, <b>Weighted LGD</b>, <b>Net Carrying Amount</b>, <b>Total ECL</b>.</li></ul><h4>What each tile means</h4><ul><li><b>Total Exposure (EAD)</b>: the sum of the carrying amount of every loan in the loan book for the period (and portfolio). EAD is Exposure at Default, the amount at risk.</li><li><b>Total ECL</b>: the sum of the calculated expected credit loss for the period. The note beneath gives the coverage.</li><li><b>ECL Coverage</b>: Total ECL divided by Total Exposure, as a percentage. This is the provision rate on the book.</li><li><b>Stage 3 Exposure</b>: the carrying amount of loans whose final stage (after qualitative overrides) is Stage 3, with the note giving its share of the book.</li><li><b>Weighted PD</b>: the average probability of default used in the ECL run for each stage, weighted by each stage\'s exposure.</li><li><b>Weighted LGD</b>: the average loss given default used for Stage 3, multiplied by Stage 3 exposure and divided by total exposure.</li><li><b>Net Carrying Amount</b> (summary table only): Total EAD less Total ECL, the book after provisions.</li></ul><h4>Change chips and status</h4><p>When a comparison period exists, each money tile shows a chip such as <b>▲ +3.2% vs 2023-11</b> and each ratio tile a chip in points such as <b>▼ -0.15pts vs 2023-11</b>. The colour reads the business meaning, not the direction: growth in exposure is favourable (green), while a rise in ECL, coverage, Stage 3 exposure, PD or LGD is adverse (red). A grey chip means no material change. No chip is shown when the earlier value is zero. In the Portfolio Summary the <b>Status</b> column applies the same logic with three grades: a move in the favourable direction is <b>Favourable</b> (green); an adverse move under 10% (or under 1 point) is <b>Watch</b> (gold); a larger adverse move is <b>Adverse</b> (red); a move under 1% (or 0.05 points) is <b>Stable</b> (grey). Hovering a chip shows the wording, for example <b>Moderate movement, keep an eye on it</b>.</p><h4>To compare two periods</h4><ol><li>Choose the later month in <b>Reporting Period</b>.</li><li>Choose the earlier month in <b>Compare To</b>, or leave <b>Previous period</b>.</li><li>Read the chips on the tiles and the <b>Change</b> and <b>Status</b> columns of the Portfolio Summary.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>The Dashboard is read-only. It reflects whatever the last ECL Calculation wrote for the period, so if a run is repeated the figures update the next time the page loads. Filters are carried in the page address, so you can bookmark or share a particular view.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>No data available. Please upload or calculate ECL first.</b> No period has a completed ECL run; the tiles show zero. Import the loan book and run ECL Calculation.</li><li><b>The period I want is missing from Reporting Period.</b> Only periods with a completed ECL run are listed.</li><li><b>Total Exposure is zero but Total ECL is not.</b> ECL results exist but the loan book rows for the period carry no carrying amount. Check the Loan Book for the period and re-run ECL.</li><li><b>Enormous percentage moves.</b> Early periods hold partial books; compare against a recent full month.</li><li><b>No data in the selected range</b> under ECL Coverage Trend: the From and To months exclude every calculated period; widen the range.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Press Dashboard in the sidebar.',
                'In the green filter bar choose the Reporting Period, a Portfolio (or All portfolios) and the Compare To period.',
                'Read the six KPI tiles: hover a tile for the exact amount and read the chip beneath it for the change against the comparison period.',
                'Read the three stage cards for exposure, ECL, PD and share of book in Stage 1, 2 and 3.',
                'Switch Portfolio Composition by Stage or ECL Coverage Trend to Table when you need the figures; adjust the trend range with the From and To selectors.',
                'Read the Portfolio Summary Status column: Favourable, Watch, Adverse or Stable.',
            ],
            'images' => ['dashboard' => 'The IFRS 9 ECL Dashboard: filter bar, six KPI tiles, stage cards, composition doughnut, coverage trend and the Portfolio Summary table'],
            'routes' => ['dashboard'],
        ],

        'Period Workspace' => [
            'body' => '<p>The IFRS 9 Period Workspace tracks the month-end close of one reporting period as a ten-step checklist and keeps the team\'s conversation about that period in one place. Analysts use it to see what is still outstanding; administrators use it to tick the two steps that need human judgement; everyone can post messages. To reach it, press <b>Workspace</b> near the top of the sidebar.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li>Page title <b>IFRS 9 Period Workspace</b>.</li><li><b>Reporting Period</b> pill (green, top right, calendar icon): every period that has a loan book, newest first. Changing it reloads the checklist and messages for that period.</li><li><b>Signed in as</b> card: your name and email and a badge reading either <b>Administrator: can tick manual steps</b> (green) or <b>Read-only view</b> (grey).</li><li><b>Progress card</b>: a ring filled in green to the percentage complete with <b>30% COMPLETE</b> in its centre, the heading <b>Close progress for 2025-11</b> and the line <b>3 of 10 steps complete. System-verified steps update automatically from the data.</b> Beneath it either an amber banner <b>7 STEP(S) OUTSTANDING</b> listing the outstanding step names, or a green banner <b>All steps complete for this period</b>.</li><li><b>Tabs</b>: <b>IFRS 9 Close Checklist</b> with a counter such as <b>3/10</b>, and <b>Team Messages</b> with the message count.</li><li><b>Checklist rows</b>, one per step, each with a numbered circle (a green tick once done), the step name (struck through once done), a detail line, and at the right: a grey <b>System</b> badge with a padlock on system-verified steps (tooltip <b>Verified automatically from the database</b>); a solid green <b>Done</b> or gold <b>Pending</b> badge; a green arrow icon titled <b>Open this screen</b> that takes you to the page where the step is done; and, for administrators on manual steps only, a gold tick titled <b>Mark as done</b> or a grey circular arrow titled <b>Reopen this step</b>.</li><li><b>Team Messages</b> tab: header <b>Team conversation</b> with <b>Period 2025-11 · visible to everyone signed in</b>; message bubbles (yours on the right in green, others on the left in grey) with the sender\'s name and a relative time; a box with the prompt <b>Message the team about this period...</b> and a green <b>Send</b> button.</li></ul><h4>The ten steps</h4><ol><li><b>Import the loan book for the period</b> (system): done when the period has loan book rows. Detail: <b>3,593 loans imported</b> or <b>No loan book rows for this period</b>.</li><li><b>Portfolio segmentation &amp; sector tags</b> (system): done when every loan has a portfolio. Detail: <b>3,593 of 3,593 loans assigned to a portfolio</b>.</li><li><b>Stage allocation (SICR rules applied)</b> (system): done when every loan has a final stage.</li><li><b>PD model applied to the loan book</b> (system): done when at least one loan carries a PD. Detail: <b>0 loans carry a PD</b>.</li><li><b>LGD model applied to the loan book</b> (system): done when at least one loan carries an LGD.</li><li><b>Forward-looking (macro) adjustment applied</b> (system): done when at least one loan carries a post-FLI PD.</li><li><b>ECL calculation run</b> (system): done when ECL result rows exist. Detail: <b>ECL not calculated for this period</b> until then.</li><li><b>Review IFRS 9 reports &amp; data quality</b> (manual): ticked by an administrator after the review.</li><li><b>Stress / sensitivity scenarios run</b> (system): done when a stress scenario has been saved. Detail: <b>No saved stress scenarios</b> until then.</li><li><b>Management sign-off for the period</b> (manual): ticked by an administrator when management has signed the period off. It has no linked screen.</li></ol><p>Steps marked <b>System</b> are verified against the database every time the page loads and can never be ticked by hand. Steps 2 to 7 show <b>Awaiting loan book</b> until step 1 is done. Manual steps show <b>Ticked by Admin · 05 Dec 2025 14:20</b> once done.</p><h4>To tick a manual step (administrators)</h4><ol><li>Choose the period in the <b>Reporting Period</b> pill.</li><li>On the <b>Review IFRS 9 reports &amp; data quality</b> or <b>Management sign-off for the period</b> row press the gold tick (<b>Mark as done</b>).</li><li>A green flash confirms: <b>Step "Management sign-off for the period" completed for 2025-11.</b></li><li>To undo, press the grey circular arrow (<b>Reopen this step</b>); the flash reads <b>reopened</b>.</li></ol><h4>To post a team message</h4><ol><li>Press the <b>Team Messages</b> tab.</li><li>Type in the box (up to 2,000 characters) and press <b>Send</b> or the Enter key. Shift with Enter starts a new line.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>Ticking or reopening a manual step is stored against the period with your name and the time, and every other administrator receives a bell notification such as <b>Admin completed "Management sign-off for the period" for 2025-11.</b> that links back to this page. Messages are visible to everyone signed in; the fifty most recent for the period are shown. Nothing in the Workspace changes loan data; it records the state of the close.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The tick icons are missing.</b> Only administrators can tick; your badge reads <b>Read-only view</b>.</li><li><b>Only administrators can update the workspace.</b> Shown as a <b>No access rights</b> dialogue if a non-administrator tries to tick a step.</li><li><b>This step is verified automatically by the system.</b> Do the work on the linked screen and the step will turn green by itself.</li><li><b>The period I need is not listed.</b> Import the loan book for it first.</li><li><b>Send is greyed out.</b> The message box is empty.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Press Workspace in the sidebar and choose the period in the Reporting Period pill.',
                'Read the progress ring and the amber banner to see how many steps are outstanding.',
                'On a Pending row press the green arrow (Open this screen) to go to the page where that step is completed; system steps turn green by themselves once the data exists.',
                'As an administrator, press the gold tick (Mark as done) on Review IFRS 9 reports & data quality and on Management sign-off for the period when they are complete.',
                'Press Team Messages, type a note for colleagues and press Send.',
            ],
            'images' => ['workspace' => 'The Period Workspace: signed-in card, progress ring with outstanding banner, and the ten-step close checklist with System, Done and Pending badges'],
            'routes' => ['workspace.index'],
        ],

        'Notifications' => [
            'body' => '<p>The bell at the top right of every page is your in-system notice board. The platform writes a notification to it whenever something happens that concerns you: a ticket you raised or were assigned is changed, or another administrator ticks a step in the Workspace. Nothing is emailed for these events; the bell is the only channel, so glance at it when you sign in.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li><b>The bell</b>: a grey outline when there is nothing unread. When you have unread notifications it sits on an amber circle, swings gently, and carries a red badge with the number unread (shown as <b>9+</b> beyond nine). The count is refreshed every time you move to another page.</li><li><b>The dropdown</b> (press the bell): a white panel headed <b>Notifications</b> with a green <b>Mark all read</b> link on the right whenever something is unread.</li><li><b>The list</b>: your eight most recent notifications, newest first. Each row has a dot (green for unread, grey for read), the message text and a relative time such as <b>2 hours ago</b>; hover the time to see the full date and time. Unread rows have a pale green background.</li><li>While the list loads it reads <b>Loading notifications...</b>; if you have never received one it reads <b>No notifications yet.</b></li><li>Press anywhere outside the panel to close it.</li></ul><h4>Which events raise a notification</h4><ul><li><b>Ticket #012 created: &lt;title&gt;</b>: sent to the person a new ticket is assigned to.</li><li><b>Ticket #012 updated (In Progress): &lt;title&gt;</b>: sent to the ticket\'s assignee and creator when its details or status are edited.</li><li><b>New update on ticket #012: &lt;first 80 characters of the note&gt;</b>: sent to the assignee and creator when a progress note is posted.</li><li><b>Admin completed "Review IFRS 9 reports &amp; data quality" for 2025-11.</b> (or <b>reopened</b>): sent to every other administrator when a manual Workspace step is ticked or reopened.</li></ul><p>You are never notified of your own action; only the other people involved are. Each notification links to the page it concerns.</p><h4>To read and clear notifications</h4><ol><li>Press the bell.</li><li>Press a row to open the ticket or workspace page it refers to. The row is marked read and the badge count drops by one.</li><li>Press <b>Mark all read</b> to clear the badge without opening each item.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>Marking a notification read only changes its dot and the badge; the notification stays in your list. The badge is recalculated by the server on every page load, so if a colleague acts while you are reading, the new count appears on your next click. Notifications are personal: no one else sees your list.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The bell never changes.</b> Nothing has been assigned to you and you are not an administrator. Ask to be set as the assignee on tickets you should follow.</li><li><b>The list is empty but the badge shows a number.</b> Press the bell again to reload the list; if it persists, refresh the page.</li><li><b>I expected an email.</b> Platform events are bell-only. The only emails the system sends are login details for new users and password reset links.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Look at the bell at the top right: amber with a red number means you have unread notifications.',
                'Press the bell to open the Notifications panel.',
                'Press a notification to go to the ticket or Workspace page it concerns; it is marked read automatically.',
                'Press Mark all read to clear the badge in one go.',
                'Press anywhere outside the panel to close it.',
            ],
            'images' => ['dashboard' => 'The notification bell sits at the top right of the header, beside the avatar'],
        ],

        'Support tickets' => [
            'body' => '<p>Support Tickets is the register of every enhancement request, issue and change raised on the platform, shared by MAIIC and the developer. Each ticket carries a unique reference such as <b>#012</b>, a category, a priority, a status, an assignee and a full activity trail, so both sides can see what was asked, who is doing it and where it stands. Anyone with the tickets permission can read the register; creating, updating and deleting need their own permissions. To reach it, open the sidebar, expand <b>ADMINISTRATION</b> and choose <b>Support Tickets</b>.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li>Page title <b>Support Tickets</b>.</li><li><b>Five count tiles</b>: <b>All</b>, <b>Open</b>, <b>In Progress</b>, <b>Resolved</b>, <b>Closed</b>. Each is a button; the selected one has a green border and filters the list to that status.</li><li><b>Filter</b> button (opens <b>Status</b> and <b>Category</b> drop-downs, each with an <b>All statuses</b> / <b>All categories</b> option), the <b>Search…</b> box (matches the reference, title or requested-by name) and <b>Reset</b>.</li><li><b>New Ticket</b>: green button at the right (reads <b>New</b> on narrow screens).</li><li><b>Table columns</b>: <b>Ref</b> (green monospaced link), <b>Title</b>, <b>Category</b>, <b>Priority</b>, <b>Status</b>, <b>Assignee</b>, <b>Updated</b>, then the row icons: green eye <b>View ticket</b>, gold pencil <b>Edit ticket</b> (opens the ticket with the details form already in edit mode), red bin <b>Delete ticket</b>.</li><li>Empty state: <b>No tickets found.</b> Pagination with <b>Previous</b> and <b>Next</b> beneath.</li><li><b>Badge colours</b>. Status: <b>Open</b> gold, <b>In Progress</b> green, <b>On Hold</b> grey, <b>Resolved</b> solid green, <b>Closed</b> light grey. Priority: <b>Low</b> grey, <b>Medium</b> green, <b>High</b> gold, <b>Critical</b> red. Category: <b>Enhancement</b> green, <b>Issue</b> red, <b>Change Request</b> gold, <b>Other</b> grey.</li></ul><h4>The New Ticket form</h4><p>The heading shows the breadcrumb <b>Support Tickets / New Ticket</b> and the line <b>This ticket will be logged as #012</b>, the next number in sequence.</p><ul><li><b>Title</b> (required, up to 255 characters): a short summary, for example <b>Loan book import rejects rows with blank branch</b>.</li><li><b>Description</b>: details, context and acceptance criteria. Optional but strongly recommended.</li><li><b>Category</b>: Enhancement (default), Issue, Change Request or Other.</li><li><b>Priority</b>: Low, Medium (default), High or Critical.</li><li><b>Status</b>: Open (default), In Progress, On Hold, Resolved or Closed.</li><li><b>Requested by</b>: who asked, for example <b>Barry (MAIIC)</b>. Optional.</li><li><b>Source</b>: how it arrived, for example <b>email</b>, <b>meeting</b>, <b>phone</b>. Optional, up to 40 characters.</li><li><b>Assign to (responsible person)</b>: <b>Unassigned</b> or any user.</li><li><b>Due date</b>: optional target date.</li><li><b>Cancel</b> returns to the list; <b>Create Ticket</b> saves.</li></ul><h4>The ticket page</h4><ul><li>Breadcrumb <b>Support Tickets / #012: title</b>.</li><li><b>Description</b> card (or <b>No description provided.</b>) with a green <b>Resolution</b> box once a resolution has been written.</li><li><b>Activity</b>: a timeline. Grey dots are system entries such as <b>Ticket logged.</b> and <b>Status changed from Open to In Progress.</b>; green dots are notes by people. Status changes show the old and new status badges with an arrow, and every entry carries the author and time. Empty state: <b>No activity yet.</b></li><li><b>Add an update</b>: a box with the prompt <b>Progress note, comment or resolution detail…</b>, a <b>Change status to</b> drop-down whose first option is <b>keep Open</b> (the current status), and the <b>Post update</b> button.</li><li><b>Details</b> card on the right with an <b>Edit</b> button (gold pencil; becomes <b>Cancel</b> while editing) and the rows <b>Status</b>, <b>Category</b>, <b>Priority</b>, <b>Assignee</b>, <b>Requested by</b>, <b>Source</b>, <b>Due</b>, <b>Created</b> and, once set, <b>Resolved</b>. In edit mode the same fields become a form with the extra <b>Resolution</b> box and a <b>Save changes</b> button.</li><li><b>Delete ticket</b>: a red-bordered button under the details.</li></ul><h4>To add a progress note or change the status</h4><ol><li>Open the ticket (green eye or press its reference).</li><li>Type the note under <b>Add an update</b> (required, up to 5,000 characters).</li><li>Leave <b>Change status to</b> on <b>keep …</b>, or choose the new status.</li><li>Press <b>Post update</b>. The flash reads <b>Update added to #012.</b></li></ol><h4>To delete a ticket</h4><ol><li>Press the red bin on the row or <b>Delete ticket</b> on the ticket page.</li><li>The dialogue asks <b>Are you sure you want to permanently delete this ticket and its activity trail?</b> Press <b>Delete Ticket</b> to confirm or <b>Nevermind</b> to keep it.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>Creating a ticket writes the first activity entry <b>Ticket logged.</b>, shows <b>Ticket #012 created successfully.</b> and opens the ticket page. Moving a ticket to Resolved or Closed stamps the <b>Resolved</b> date; moving it back clears the date. Every create, update, note and delete is written to the Audit Trail (<b>Create Ticket #012</b>, <b>Update Ticket #012</b>, <b>Comment on Ticket #012</b>, <b>Delete Ticket #012</b>) and sends a bell notification to the ticket\'s assignee and creator, other than the person acting. References are never reused.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>New Ticket, the pencil or the bin is missing.</b> Your role lacks the create, update or delete permission for tickets.</li><li><b>The title field is required.</b> Enter a title before pressing <b>Create Ticket</b>.</li><li><b>The source must not be greater than 40 characters.</b> Shorten the Source text.</li><li><b>The body field is required.</b> A progress note cannot be empty; type the note before <b>Post update</b>.</li><li><b>I cannot find a ticket.</b> Press <b>All</b> and <b>Reset</b> to clear the status and category filters, then search by reference number without the hash.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Open the sidebar, expand ADMINISTRATION and choose Support Tickets.',
                'Press New Ticket. Note the reference shown after This ticket will be logged as.',
                'Type a clear Title and a Description with details and what a good outcome looks like.',
                'Choose the Category, Priority and Status; enter Requested by and Source; choose the responsible person under Assign to and a Due date if there is one.',
                'Press Create Ticket. The ticket page opens with the entry Ticket logged. in its Activity.',
                'To report progress later, open the ticket, type under Add an update, choose Change status to if the status moves, and press Post update.',
            ],
            'images' => [
                'tickets' => 'The Support Tickets register: count tiles, Filter and Search…, the ticket table with category, priority and status badges, and the row icons',
                'tickets-create' => 'The New Ticket form with its reference, Title, Description, Category, Priority, Status, Requested by, Source, Assign to and Due date',
            ],
            'routes' => ['tickets.index', 'tickets.create', 'tickets.show'],
        ],
    ],
];
